  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light suffers minimum deviation when incident on a prism having angle of the prism equal to $60^{\\circ}$. The refractive index of the prism material is $\\sqrt{2}$. The angle of incidence (in degrees) is ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "45",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mu=\\frac{\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{A}+\\delta_{\\mathrm{m}}}{2}\\right)}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{A}}{2}\\right)}, \\text { since } \\mathrm{A}=60^{\\circ} \\quad \\therefore \\delta \\mathrm{m}=30^{\\circ} \\\\ & \\delta_{\\mathrm{m}}=2 \\mathrm{i}-\\mathrm{A}[\\text { as } \\mathrm{i}=\\mathrm{e}] \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{i}=45^{\\circ}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}